text:
Priya: Quick find from the user report: examples under /docs/guides/function-calling/ show `response_schema` and `callTool()` — those are outdated. Can we standardize to the v1 names and add a clear migration blurb?
Dan: Thanks — I spotted that too when testing the quickstart. I'm happy to update the snippets.
Tom: I can handle the schema side. Do we want a single canonical schema example that we encourage, or multiple (strict/lenient)?
Priya: single canonical strict example + a tiny "lenient" note. Recommend strict by default (so people won't accidentally accept extra fields).
Dan: Proposed SDK example (v1):
```js
// v1: invokeTool
const result = await client.invokeTool('classify', {
  input: text,
  params: { temperature: 0 }
});
// result.output is the model return (string)
```
Tom: For schema, here's a short strict example to paste: 
```json
{
  "type": "object",
  "properties": {
    "label": { "type": "string" },
    "confidence": { "type": "number" }
  },
  "required": ["label"],
  "additionalProperties": false
}
```
Alex: Nice. Add a `confidence` range note (0-1) in prose. Also show a tiny JS validation flow so readers know how to handle parse problems.
Dan: Validation snippet suggestion:
```js
try {
  const parsed = JSON.parse(result.output);
  validate(parsed, schema); // returns true or throws
} catch (err) {
  // return safe default or call model again with clearer system prompt
}
```
Priya: Perfect. Also include a short migration bullet: "If migrating from v0.x, rename `response_schema` -> `outputSchema` and `callTool()` -> `invokeTool()`; see example." Keep it one line inside the guide header.
Tom: One more thing: prefix caching can make deterministic tool outputs stale in long-lived sessions. Add a one-sentence warning and link to caching docs.
Alex: I'll add: "If you rely on deterministic tool outputs, consider disabling prefix cache for that route or use cache-busting keys." Link: https://docs.redwood.ai/guides/caching#prefix-kv
Priya: Can someone fix the two broken links in the guide TOC? They point to old paths under /integrations.
Dan: I'll include link fixes in my branch. Branch: docs/tooling/migrate-v1-snippets. PR created: https://github.com/redwood-inference/docs/pull/490
Tom: I opened docs/schema/strict-examples branch with updated JSON and a small fixture test. PR: https://github.com/redwood-inference/docs/pull/491
Docs Bot: Scheduled jobs: docs/link-check on PR #490, docs/schema-lint on PR #491.
PreviewBot: Preview builds queued for PRs #490 and #491. Preview URL: https://preview.docs.redwood.ai/pr-490-491/ (valid 48h)
Dan: CI flagged a markdown lint issue (trailing spaces) on #490, fixed and pushed.
Tom: Schema lint passed locally; added a test case showing a missing required field causing helpful error message.
Alex: I've added the migration blurb to the top of the page and a changelog item under "Docs" in the next release notes.
Priya: Review checklist: 1) confirm SDK snippet uses the canonical client API 2) schema is copy/pasteable 3) caching note + link added 4) TOC links fixed 5) PRs have passing checks.
Dan: I'm running a quick smoke test on the preview — will report back in 15.
Tom: I'm going to add a tiny note about using `additionalProperties: false` to avoid surprises when mapping to typed languages.
Alex: Approved the wording for migration and caching.
Dan: Smoke test OK. LGTM.
Tom: Merged #491; #490 merged after green CI.
Priya: Thank you! Closing thread. :tada:
